1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Father possibilities:
2 CONT 1) Benjamin Hansen: son til skipper Hans Steensen Mogelbostadt (betalte skatt der i 1610); nevnt i bygdebok ogsaa der en skipper Benjamin Hansen: https://www.nb.no/items/a64d1866af0c2b942de8c77a46d7917d?page=161&searchText=Benjami
2 CONC n
2 CONT * Bygdefar-skippere paa Myklebostad: Gregus Olsen, Jens Gregussen, Jens Larsen, Christen Michelborg og '''Benjamin Hansen'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT vvvv---------------------------------------------- Prior Theories ----------------------------------vvvv
2 CONT
2 CONT Feil: Benjamin Aronsen (ca1643): It cannot be that Ole Benjaminsen (f.bef. 1620) was the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Benjamin-Myklebostad/6000000007402699651 (f~1643) and Rakel Andersdatter (f~1660).  According to [https://
2 CONC www.nb.no/items/a64d1866af0c2b942de8c77a46d7917d?page=163&searchText=samuelsdatter "Nesna Bygdebok 1" page 160], Rachel Andersdatter was first married to Benjamin Aronsen b. 1641, and after his death married to Gregus Jensen. <br/
2 CONC >
2 CONT In the book [https://www.nb.no/items/719a238b8822de8622a5535fc7f22e9d?page=39 "Skifter fra Nesna 1686-1780" page 36], which is an index of probates, when she died she is not listed as having a son by the name of Ole.
