1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HANS LARSEN, STILVASSTRAND
2 CONT
2 CONT Karen Maria Olsdatter was married 20 July 1846 to Hans Larsen and they were farmers in Stillvasstranda in Rana, Nordland, Norway. Alltogether they had eight sons and one daughter: Ellen Johan, Olaus, Lars, Didrik Julius, Constanse
2 CONC  Emilie, Lorentz Edvard, Heitman Kristian, Andreas Olaus og Carl Martin.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family had some hard times. Their son Lars died the same year he was born, in 1851. Karen Maries both parents died in 1959. In fact, her father shot himself after her mother had died. Hanss mother died in 1961. Hans Larsson hi
2 CONC mself died in 1862 of watering in his body, possibly because of a heart condition or malnutrition. His wife Karen Marie died a year later in birth, leaving the new born twins as well as the other seven siblings as orphans.
2 CONT
2 CONT The oldest son, Ellen Johan started to work, became a boatbuilder, farmer and carpenter, married and lived with his family in Nordland, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Olaus, the second oldest child, worked for some tima and left Norway in 1876, to seek a better fortune in USA. Olaus accompanied his niece, Hilda Didriksdatter Hanson, from Trondheim to Liverpool to Boston in 1905. Hildas father D
2 CONC idrik was a cobbler and farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT The only girl in the family, Constanse, was 8 years old when her mother died. She came in foster care with Johan from Toftlia. He took over the farm in Fisktjönnmoen under Fagerjord from his uncle in 1850. Johan was married to Ber
2 CONC it Larsdatter from Fagerjord. They had no children. I dont know what happened to Constanse after 1865.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lorentz was 5 years old when his mother died. I haven’t found him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Heitman was 4 years old when he became an orphan. I have found one Heitman Kristian Hansen that died in Tromsø in 1942, but I am not sure about it is the same man.
2 CONT
2 CONT The newborn twins, Andreas Olaus and Carl Martin, got separated and was placed in foster care. Andreas Olaus died only 14 years old, of Tuberculosis. Carl Martin got married and had many children. He was among other things working
2 CONC  with cement.
2 CONT
2 CONT SAT, Ministerialprotokoller, klokkerbøker og fødselsregistre - Nordland, 827/L0392: Ministerialbok nr. 827A04, 1853-1866, s. 212 Brukslenke for sidevisning: https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20050427031042
